      "content": "The culprit behind the stinging sensation when cutting onions is a compound called Syn-propanethial-S-oxide, also known as allyl sulfide. When the onion is cut, cells containing this compound are broken and released into the air as a gas. This gas reacts with water on the surface of the eyes to form sulfuric acid, which irritates the eyes and causes the stinging sensation. This process is known as \"gas-sensing\" and is extremely efficient due to the high concentration of the compound in onions.",
